PATIENT: Doctor, it hurts when I bend my arm like this!
DOCTOR:  Then don't!

Why on earth would you want to pick up 15 orcish helms, 17 scimitars,
and 87 rocks?  The moral of the story is, don't get so overburdened in
the first place.

>I accept that there are more altars, more artifacts and more 'quick
>benefits' in 3.1 but this kind of thing (AND those bloody invisible
>bloody gnomes with their bloody invisible wands of bloody invisible
>fire!) make portions of the game almost unplayable. 

'Sfunny, I find it quite playable, and extremely enjoyable.  Another
tip: don't go down into the Gnomish Mines until you're high enough
level.  I know that the stairs into them are usually found at level 2 or
3, but I recommend waiting until your character is level 7 or 8.  Then
come back up and clean out the mines.  Works fine for me.  Invisible
gnomes with wands of fire are very rare in the upper levels of the
Dungeons of Doom, but are all-too-common in the Gnomish mines.

Would you descend into Hell without fire resistance?  No?  Then why do
you want to go into the Gnomish Mines before you're ready?
